1
00:00:00,860 --> 00:00:02,660
Wealth, Fame, Power.

2
00:00:02,940 --> 00:00:04,577
Gold Roger, the King of the Pirates,

3
00:00:04,660 --> 00:00:07,197
attained this and everything
else the world had to offer.

4
00:00:07,280 --> 00:00:10,456
And his dying words drove
countless souls to the seas.

5
00:00:10,740 --> 00:00:11,975
You want my treasure?

6
00:00:12,220 --> 00:00:13,420
You can have it.

7
00:00:13,620 --> 00:00:16,620
I left everything I gathered
together in one place.

8
00:00:16,920 --> 00:00:19,060
Now you just have to find it.

9
00:00:20,940 --> 00:00:24,237
These words lured men to
the Grand Line in pursuit

10
00:00:24,320 --> 00:00:26,757
of dreams greater than
they'd ever dared to imagine.

11
00:00:26,840 --> 00:00:29,517
This is the time known
as the Great Pirate Era.

12
00:00:29,600 --> 00:00:35,140
Come aboard and bring along
all your hopes and dreams

13
00:00:35,700 --> 00:00:40,440
Together we will find everything
that we're looking for

14
00:00:41,520 --> 00:00:42,700
One piece

15
00:00:47,920 --> 00:00:50,177
Compass left behind,

16
00:00:50,260 --> 00:00:55,217
it'll only slow us down Your
heart will be your guide,

17
00:00:55,300 --> 00:00:58,457
raise the sails and take the helm

18
00:00:58,540 --> 00:01:02,497
That legendary place That the end

19
00:01:02,580 --> 00:01:06,657
of the map reveals Is only legendary

20
00:01:06,740 --> 00:01:10,117
Until someone proves it real

21
00:01:10,200 --> 00:01:15,697
Through it all Through all the trouble
and times Through the heartache

22
00:01:15,780 --> 00:01:21,380
and through the pain Know that
I will be there to stand by you

23
00:01:21,900 --> 00:01:24,240
Just like I know you'll stand by me

24
00:01:25,220 --> 00:01:29,277
so come aboard and bring along all your

25
00:01:29,360 --> 00:01:33,197
hopes and dreams together we will find

26
00:01:33,280 --> 00:01:37,957
everything that we're looking for there's

27
00:01:38,040 --> 00:01:42,420
always room for you if
you want to be my friend

28
00:01:50,460 --> 00:01:51,290
Hey, man.

29
00:01:51,500 --> 00:01:53,500
You all right? Try to breathe.

30
00:01:53,880 --> 00:01:55,527
You need a little fresh air.

31
00:01:55,740 --> 00:01:56,799
You want a pillow?

32
00:01:56,980 --> 00:01:59,580
Or maybe some water? Speak.

33
00:02:01,980 --> 00:02:03,760
This is bad. You know what?

34
00:02:03,860 --> 00:02:05,577
I make a great banana pudding.

35
00:02:05,660 --> 00:02:06,490
Want some?

36
00:02:06,573 --> 00:02:07,403
You idiot.

37
00:02:07,486 --> 00:02:09,657
We don't want him to choke to death
on any of your culinary disasters.

38
00:02:09,740 --> 00:02:13,097
Better that than the trots he'd get from
choking down one of your raunchy meat pies.

39
00:02:13,180 --> 00:02:16,637
The reason I won't feed him one of my
meat pies is because after one bite,

40
00:02:16,720 --> 00:02:18,955
he'd think he died and gone to heaven.

41
00:02:19,680 --> 00:02:20,510
Ah!

42
00:02:20,593 --> 00:02:21,423
Don't die yet!

43
00:02:23,680 --> 00:02:26,700
Well, this isn't good. We're in trouble.

44
00:02:26,940 --> 00:02:28,380
No, that was just luck.

45
00:02:28,600 --> 00:02:31,937
Don Krieg is going to get up
and kick his ass any minute now.

46
00:02:32,020 --> 00:02:32,850
Just watch.

47
00:02:33,440 --> 00:02:34,440
Hope he's dead.

48
00:02:36,180 --> 00:02:39,380
So, boy, it's not your funeral yet, is it?

49
00:02:39,720 --> 00:02:40,660
Too bad.

50
00:02:44,040 --> 00:02:46,297
Because one of us has got to go.

51
00:02:46,380 --> 00:02:53,040
Oh, and since I'm here, I'd
really like to pay my respects!

52
00:02:53,980 --> 00:02:55,360
Go to hell!

53
00:02:58,380 --> 00:02:59,220
You bitch!

54
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:04,760
This can't be happening!

55
00:03:05,020 --> 00:03:06,491
He's taking another fall!

56
00:03:08,480 --> 00:03:09,920
But how?

57
00:03:10,260 --> 00:03:12,277
I've never seen anyone
hit him because they're

58
00:03:12,360 --> 00:03:14,097
usually dead before they get close enough!

59
00:03:14,180 --> 00:03:17,980
The fact is, he might not
actually be invincible

60
00:03:20,060 --> 00:03:22,200
What the hell are you?

61
00:03:24,280 --> 00:03:26,720
Look at that, the kid's pretty good.

62
00:03:27,520 --> 00:03:28,877
Yeah, no kidding.

63
00:03:28,960 --> 00:03:30,657
He's amazing.

64
00:03:30,740 --> 00:03:32,317
Finish him off, Chaw Boy.

65
00:03:32,400 --> 00:03:34,397
Yeah, end it once and for all.

66
00:03:34,480 --> 00:03:37,957
That punk is fighting with Don Krieg
as if he were the same strength.

67
00:03:38,040 --> 00:03:40,897
This can't be real, it's like
I'm watching my own nightmare.

68
00:03:40,980 --> 00:03:42,917
He's supposed to be truly invincible.

69
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:46,297
Well, if he gets beaten by this little
kid, his reputation will be completely...

70
00:03:46,380 --> 00:03:47,560
Shut up, maggots!

71
00:03:47,720 --> 00:03:48,700
Never doubt me!

72
00:03:56,160 --> 00:03:57,800
What was that?

73
00:03:59,660 --> 00:04:03,248
Finally, he's gonna stop messing
around and step up his game!

74
00:04:03,480 --> 00:04:05,200
The mighty Battlespear!

75
00:04:05,840 --> 00:04:07,040
What was that?

76
00:04:07,340 --> 00:04:08,458
An exploding spear?

77
00:04:09,100 --> 00:04:10,060
Now what?

78
00:04:10,260 --> 00:04:12,160
You gonna try to hide from me?

79
00:04:13,340 --> 00:04:14,580
All right, then, boy.

80
00:04:14,800 --> 00:04:15,940
This should be fun.

81
00:04:16,460 --> 00:04:18,020
My mighty battle spear.

82
00:04:18,360 --> 00:04:21,277
It's different from the one
I was fighting with earlier.

83
00:04:21,360 --> 00:04:25,184
When this thing hits you, you
won't just be wounded and flailing.

84
00:04:25,620 --> 00:04:27,796
You will be blown straight into hell!

85
00:04:30,520 --> 00:04:32,049
That's not a normal spear!

86
00:04:32,860 --> 00:04:33,697
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa!

87
00:04:33,780 --> 00:04:34,610
Not in the water!

88
00:04:34,693 --> 00:04:35,523
Not in the water!

89
00:04:36,400 --> 00:04:38,020
That spear really sucks!

90
00:04:38,200 --> 00:04:40,553
It explodes every time he hits anything!

91
00:04:42,200 --> 00:04:44,300
what's going on my knees

92
00:04:46,520 --> 00:04:51,117
he's lost way too much blood he
can't fight for much longer this

93
00:04:51,200 --> 00:04:57,137
better end quickly you look tired
too bad guess you should have saved a

94
00:04:57,220 --> 00:05:02,657
little more energy damn if everything
rocking i can't hit him with full

95
00:05:02,740 --> 00:05:08,300
force i've never in my life seen a
more stunning weapon than the mighty

96
00:05:09,020 --> 00:05:09,850
battle spear.

97
00:05:09,933 --> 00:05:12,897
Don Krieg is the only one strong
enough to handle the spear,

98
00:05:12,980 --> 00:05:16,277
since the harder he strikes with it,
the bigger the explosion it causes.

99
00:05:16,360 --> 00:05:20,831
Anyone else would just be completely
destroyed by their own pathetic attack.

100
00:05:25,940 --> 00:05:26,780
It's strength.

101
00:05:27,080 --> 00:05:28,457
His strength is the key.

102
00:05:28,540 --> 00:05:30,977
He causes the kind of
damage no one else can,

103
00:05:31,060 --> 00:05:32,617
because there's just no
one else who can swing

104
00:05:32,700 --> 00:05:35,229
a spear that easily
weighs more than a ton.

105
00:05:35,380 --> 00:05:39,640
That's exactly why Don Krieg is the
most dangerous man in the East Blue.

106
00:05:51,720 --> 00:05:52,660
Now die!

107
00:05:53,960 --> 00:05:55,320
Char-Boy, look out!

108
00:05:57,180 --> 00:05:59,480
Phew, that was really close.

109
00:06:03,960 --> 00:06:06,060
YOU'RE JUST LIKE A LITTLE BUCK!

110
00:06:17,740 --> 00:06:18,570
Choreboy!

111
00:06:32,900 --> 00:06:33,800
That's rough.

112
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:37,600
I'm not finished with you.

113
00:06:37,860 --> 00:06:41,919
If you hadn't made me so angry, I
would have killed you more quickly.

114
00:06:42,500 --> 00:06:43,330
Damn it.

115
00:06:43,760 --> 00:06:47,054
There's no way that Choreboy
can take much more of this.

116
00:06:47,440 --> 00:06:49,257
That spear is way too powerful.

117
00:06:49,340 --> 00:06:50,317
Now you're wrong.

118
00:06:50,400 --> 00:06:52,871
Even with a hundred thousand more weapons,

119
00:06:53,020 --> 00:06:55,277
our chore boy can still
bring him to his knees?

120
00:06:55,360 --> 00:06:57,300
because he does not know fear.

121
00:07:13,020 --> 00:07:13,850
Ha!

122
00:07:13,933 --> 00:07:14,920
That was too easy.

123
00:07:25,460 --> 00:07:27,280
Now that's impressive.

124
00:07:36,300 --> 00:07:38,380
Stand or fall, life or death.

125
00:07:38,880 --> 00:07:41,077
In a struggle for your very existence,

126
00:07:41,160 --> 00:07:44,937
you cannot have even the slightest
bit of fear or you will be lost.

127
00:07:45,020 --> 00:07:46,608
What are you talking about?

128
00:07:46,800 --> 00:07:48,440
That kid out there...

129
00:07:59,280 --> 00:08:00,920
When he's fighting...

130
00:08:04,020 --> 00:08:06,120
He's not afraid of anything.

131
00:08:07,360 --> 00:08:09,260
Not even death.

132
00:08:21,200 --> 00:08:24,180
Is it just instinct or all a plan?

133
00:08:26,520 --> 00:08:28,217
We'll know soon!

134
00:08:28,300 --> 00:08:29,640
If he lives?

135
00:08:32,720 --> 00:08:34,137
What plan?

136
00:08:34,220 --> 00:08:35,580
Killing himself.

137
00:08:46,760 --> 00:08:48,920
You son of a bitch!

138
00:08:54,480 --> 00:08:56,237
Way to go, Chowboy!

139
00:08:56,320 --> 00:08:58,360
Do it again! Kick his ass!

140
00:09:01,500 --> 00:09:04,600
I told you, today is your funeral!

141
00:09:19,600 --> 00:09:23,140
There is no doubt that Krieg
and his pirates are strong.

142
00:09:23,460 --> 00:09:26,180
But Chorboy has something
they'll never have.

143
00:09:30,280 --> 00:09:34,880
Krieg may have more pirates at his
command than anyone else before him.

144
00:09:36,320 --> 00:09:41,997
He may have terrible weapons that cause
mass destruction to everything in his path.

145
00:09:42,080 --> 00:09:47,220
But he will never have that kid's heart.

146
00:09:57,760 --> 00:09:58,590
What?!

147
00:09:58,673 --> 00:09:59,560
My Battlespear!

148
00:09:59,740 --> 00:10:01,640
What the hell did you do?!

149
00:10:08,740 --> 00:10:11,540
I just punched it in the head five times.

150
00:10:12,120 --> 00:10:13,460
It looks tired.

151
00:10:13,800 --> 00:10:15,094
Maybe it needs a rest.

152
00:10:18,280 --> 00:10:20,100
Now it's my turn.

153
00:10:23,500 --> 00:10:26,377
Now that your little toy's
broken you're nothing to me.

154
00:10:26,460 --> 00:10:31,857
Oh yeah yeah without the
blade it's just a bomb

155
00:10:31,940 --> 00:10:34,717
on a stick and let's face
it that's pretty lame.

156
00:10:34,800 --> 00:10:36,017
You think so?

157
00:10:36,100 --> 00:10:36,957
Sure do.

158
00:10:37,040 --> 00:10:40,257
Fine so what if it is?

159
00:10:40,340 --> 00:10:43,817
Just a bomb on a stick
you're in sad shape kiddo.

160
00:10:43,900 --> 00:10:46,782
I think it'll be more than
enough to blow you to.

161
00:10:47,140 --> 00:10:47,970
You know it?

162
00:10:48,053 --> 00:10:51,877
Sounds to me like this is some sort
of pathetic attempt at a block.

163
00:10:51,960 --> 00:10:53,360
Okay but you're wrong.

164
00:10:55,420 --> 00:10:57,126
Your boy is pretty good, huh?

165
00:10:57,320 --> 00:10:59,340
He might be able to pull it off

166
00:11:00,120 --> 00:11:01,340
This is terrible.

167
00:11:01,600 --> 00:11:04,040
He just shattered the mighty battle spear

168
00:11:09,760 --> 00:11:13,137
It's a miracle he's still alive
after that many explosions.

169
00:11:13,220 --> 00:11:14,926
There's no way he can hold up

170
00:11:16,900 --> 00:11:18,140
Just give up.

171
00:11:18,300 --> 00:11:19,712
Your defeat is imminent.

172
00:11:19,980 --> 00:11:24,880
You see, when you defy me, you
sign your own death warrant!

173
00:11:30,740 --> 00:11:32,360
Hey, up here!

174
00:11:33,120 --> 00:11:33,950
Bastard!

175
00:11:34,060 --> 00:11:34,900
You monkey!

176
00:11:41,980 --> 00:11:43,260
Bounce out of that!

177
00:11:48,520 --> 00:11:50,040
Nice try!

178
00:11:53,480 --> 00:11:55,860
How many weapons does that guy have?

179
00:12:05,420 --> 00:12:07,880
Now come Tom!

180
00:12:26,780 --> 00:12:28,780
I'm wearing wood-steel body armor.

181
00:12:28,880 --> 00:12:31,380
This stuff is practically indestructible.

182
00:12:34,140 --> 00:12:37,080
We'll see about that Tom-Tom pistol!

183
00:12:46,660 --> 00:12:47,490
DONE!

184
00:12:50,380 --> 00:12:51,210
How dare you!

185
00:12:57,440 --> 00:12:58,540
It's useless.

186
00:12:58,800 --> 00:13:00,280
You'll never defeat me!

187
00:13:00,720 --> 00:13:03,077
This armor could take a
million more of your monkey

188
00:13:03,160 --> 00:13:05,925
punches and it wouldn't
have so much as a dent!

189
00:13:07,920 --> 00:13:10,200
Well, we'll just see about that.

190
00:13:12,400 --> 00:13:13,340
He's gone!

191
00:13:14,960 --> 00:13:16,240
I'm right here.

192
00:13:21,820 --> 00:13:23,740
You don't stand a chance, boy.

193
00:13:24,020 --> 00:13:26,097
Real power comes from deadly weapons.

194
00:13:26,180 --> 00:13:28,298
They're the source of true strength.

195
00:13:28,680 --> 00:13:31,180
See, only the strong are meant to live.

196
00:13:31,580 --> 00:13:32,960
And that's me.

197
00:13:37,080 --> 00:13:38,780
Yeah, that's what you think!

198
00:13:41,920 --> 00:13:43,160
It's useless!

199
00:13:44,140 --> 00:13:46,680
Foolish pride will only get you so far!

200
00:13:51,340 --> 00:13:52,170
Bazooka!

201
00:14:04,100 --> 00:14:05,060
That's it?

202
00:14:05,260 --> 00:14:08,025
After all that big talk,
that's all you've got?

203
00:14:10,080 --> 00:14:10,910
No!

204
00:14:11,140 --> 00:14:12,177
I don't believe it!

205
00:14:12,260 --> 00:14:13,436
My armor's cracking!

206
00:14:15,960 --> 00:14:18,000
It doesn't matter.

207
00:14:18,400 --> 00:14:20,540
You're done for, Shura Boy!

208
00:14:25,860 --> 00:14:27,220
It's a trap!

209
00:14:27,420 --> 00:14:28,320
Get out!

210
00:14:37,180 --> 00:14:39,040
Shoot! Shortball!

211
00:14:53,320 --> 00:14:55,160
He's not afraid of anything.

212
00:14:55,740 --> 00:14:57,700
Not even death.

213
00:14:58,320 --> 00:15:01,180
Is it just instinct, or all a plan?

214
00:15:02,700 --> 00:15:05,540
We'll know soon if he lives.

215
00:15:08,220 --> 00:15:09,440
What the?

216
00:15:29,260 --> 00:15:30,090
Oh!

217
00:15:42,300 --> 00:15:44,060
Way to go, Chowboy!

218
00:15:47,040 --> 00:15:49,180
I totally win!

219
00:15:52,920 --> 00:15:55,080
This isn't over yet, boy!

220
00:15:55,380 --> 00:15:56,520
Whoa, he's alive!

221
00:16:04,960 --> 00:16:06,280
You can't escape!

222
00:16:06,480 --> 00:16:07,580
It's a steel net!

223
00:16:19,100 --> 00:16:20,060
It's over!

224
00:16:20,400 --> 00:16:22,620
That's the ocean down there below us!

225
00:16:22,880 --> 00:16:26,704
It looks like I'll be getting the
last laugh after all, char boy!

226
00:16:30,540 --> 00:16:32,060
Take him down, dog!

227
00:16:32,340 --> 00:16:33,977
Make that little brat pay!

228
00:16:34,060 --> 00:16:35,180
Hey, get him!

229
00:16:39,260 --> 00:16:41,820
Now I got that jerk
right where I want him!

230
00:16:42,140 --> 00:16:44,060
He hasn't even flinched.

231
00:16:45,740 --> 00:16:47,560
How can he stay so cold?

232
00:16:49,620 --> 00:16:51,540
Time for me to end this!

233
00:16:51,640 --> 00:16:52,620
Right now!

234
00:16:58,320 --> 00:16:59,860
Now, Kuma Kuma!

235
00:17:12,320 --> 00:17:13,300
Giant hammer!

236
00:17:35,680 --> 00:17:36,510
No!

237
00:17:36,720 --> 00:17:38,132
Tang Creek was defeated!

238
00:17:38,520 --> 00:17:40,226
How could this have happened?

239
00:17:41,560 --> 00:17:43,860
You're awesome, Choreboy! Yay!

240
00:17:44,040 --> 00:17:45,099
He kicked his ass!

241
00:17:47,200 --> 00:17:48,080
He won!

242
00:17:48,300 --> 00:17:50,220
He really won! Oh, wow!

243
00:17:51,100 --> 00:17:52,460
I gotta be dreaming!

244
00:17:52,780 --> 00:17:54,557
That's Tang Creek we're talking about!

245
00:17:54,640 --> 00:17:55,470
I know!

246
00:17:55,553 --> 00:17:57,911
Who'd have thought that kid had it in him?

247
00:17:58,860 --> 00:18:01,560
What is it? What's going on? Hey!

248
00:18:01,980 --> 00:18:02,960
Rise and shine!

249
00:18:03,340 --> 00:18:04,340
Craig was beaten!

250
00:18:04,520 --> 00:18:06,457
Bet you never thought you'd see the day!

251
00:18:06,540 --> 00:18:07,370
What?

252
00:18:22,760 --> 00:18:26,820
Are you done daydreaming
yet? Come on! Save that, kid!

253
00:18:28,320 --> 00:18:29,280
He can't swim!

254
00:18:30,240 --> 00:18:31,070
What?

255
00:18:31,400 --> 00:18:34,797
Those with the power of the
Devil Fruit are hated by the sea,

256
00:18:34,880 --> 00:18:36,857
so they lose their ability to swim.

257
00:18:36,940 --> 00:18:37,770
What are you saying?

258
00:18:37,853 --> 00:18:38,683
He'll just sink?

259
00:18:38,820 --> 00:18:41,557
You could have told me that
sooner, you worthless old geezer!

260
00:18:41,640 --> 00:18:43,464
What if it's already too late?!

261
00:19:16,200 --> 00:19:21,337
you said you wouldn't die
you truly believe that

262
00:19:21,420 --> 00:19:26,880
right well you'll have
to do better than that

263
00:19:28,320 --> 00:19:30,460
If you want to beat me...

264
00:19:32,600 --> 00:19:35,835
Because I don't think it's
time for me to die just yet!

265
00:19:40,960 --> 00:19:42,080
These guys...

266
00:19:43,080 --> 00:19:43,910
Zoro!

267
00:19:48,620 --> 00:19:51,297
Now this fight would end
was clear from the start.

268
00:19:51,380 --> 00:19:52,380
Why choose death?

269
00:19:52,720 --> 00:19:54,000
Don't be stupid!

270
00:19:54,340 --> 00:19:56,320
Give up your ambition and live!

271
00:20:19,180 --> 00:20:24,120
I don't know, but I will not run.

272
00:20:24,860 --> 00:20:30,160
Even if I retreat a single step, I would
be shattering the promises I've made.

273
00:20:30,360 --> 00:20:31,260
I can't run.

274
00:20:31,600 --> 00:20:33,320
I would lose my honor.

275
00:20:33,940 --> 00:20:37,646
You see, without that, there
would be nothing left for me here.

276
00:20:38,320 --> 00:20:40,840
Even with a hundred thousand more weapons,

277
00:20:41,420 --> 00:20:43,777
our chore boy can still
bring him to his knees?

278
00:20:43,860 --> 00:20:45,980
because he does not know fear.

279
00:20:46,860 --> 00:20:49,317
Krieg may have more
pirates at his command.

280
00:20:49,400 --> 00:20:54,940
He may have terrible weapons that cause
mass destruction to everything in his path.

281
00:21:01,800 --> 00:21:04,840
Hey, Choreboy, don't you die on me!

282
00:21:05,560 --> 00:21:07,220
Don, are you okay?

283
00:21:07,980 --> 00:21:09,940
Please, tell us it's an act!

284
00:21:11,000 --> 00:21:12,980
Don Krieg has been defeated.

285
00:21:13,580 --> 00:21:15,000
This can't be happening.

286
00:21:15,400 --> 00:21:17,760
He's the mighty ruler of the East Blue.

287
00:21:18,300 --> 00:21:20,477
Yeah, well now he's down for the count.

288
00:21:20,560 --> 00:21:22,377
Have a look at him and see for yourself.

289
00:21:22,460 --> 00:21:24,797
That fancy armor of his got all busted up,

290
00:21:24,880 --> 00:21:27,217
and he was out as soon as he hit the deck.

291
00:21:27,300 --> 00:21:29,017
What, do you think we're lying to you?

292
00:21:29,100 --> 00:21:30,180
Go ahead and look.

293
00:21:31,780 --> 00:21:34,600
He was the only man I ever really admired.

294
00:21:35,060 --> 00:21:37,120
How foolish. Now he's lost.

295
00:21:44,940 --> 00:21:46,680
Hey, hold on.

296
00:21:46,940 --> 00:21:49,157
If you move now, the poison will set in.

297
00:21:49,240 --> 00:21:51,120
Hey, buddy, don't die.

298
00:21:52,860 --> 00:21:53,690
Chore boy.

299
00:21:53,960 --> 00:21:55,548
Chore boy, can you hear me?

300
00:21:55,920 --> 00:21:56,820
Don't die.

301
00:21:57,300 --> 00:22:00,337
You still have a lot of
things to do with your life.

302
00:22:00,420 --> 00:22:01,840
Please don't die!

303
00:22:09,980 --> 00:22:11,120
Are you kidding?

304
00:22:13,500 --> 00:22:15,620
You really are something else. No!

305
00:22:15,880 --> 00:22:17,100
I'm the strongest!

306
00:22:17,920 --> 00:22:18,980
I win!

307
00:22:19,640 --> 00:22:20,640
I'm the greatest!

308
00:22:20,900 --> 00:22:21,900
I'm the best!

309
00:22:22,060 --> 00:22:23,320
No one defeats me!

310
00:22:24,700 --> 00:22:25,530
No!

311
00:22:25,613 --> 00:22:27,120
Just stay down! Stop him!

312
00:22:27,300 --> 00:22:28,712
He's not even conscious!

313
00:22:30,840 --> 00:22:32,640
Please, don't! Stop!

314
00:22:33,700 --> 00:22:35,400
I have to win!

315
00:22:35,600 --> 00:22:36,480
I have to!

316
00:22:48,360 --> 00:22:49,880
Kill! Enemy!

317
00:22:53,160 --> 00:22:55,700
I'll fight until victory is mine!

318
00:23:01,760 --> 00:23:04,880
Don Krieg, we lost.

319
00:23:06,480 --> 00:23:07,310
Commander!

320
00:23:08,460 --> 00:23:11,754
Let's leave now, while we
still have a shred of dignity.

321
00:23:14,840 --> 00:23:17,000
Thanks for everything, Sanji.

322
00:23:17,520 --> 00:23:20,260
Sure, now leave and don't ever come back.

323
00:23:21,300 --> 00:23:24,877
Hey, Sanji, you don't owe me any favors.

324
00:23:24,960 --> 00:23:27,000
But when the kid wakes up,

325
00:23:27,200 --> 00:23:33,720
tell him I said I'll see
him on the Grand Line.

326
00:23:35,680 --> 00:23:36,560
But you...

327
00:23:37,400 --> 00:23:39,697
That's where I want to go
with the time I have left.

328
00:23:39,780 --> 00:23:41,237
It's the only thing I care about.

329
00:23:41,320 --> 00:23:43,379
The only thing that keeps me going.

330
00:23:44,020 --> 00:23:48,961
It would seem that Donkring's obsession
with the Grand Line has become mine as well.

331
00:23:54,160 --> 00:23:54,990
It's silly.

332
00:23:55,460 --> 00:23:58,540
I know that, but it's my dream.

333
00:23:59,400 --> 00:24:03,520
With this poison in my veins, I
may only have a few hours to live.

334
00:24:04,080 --> 00:24:10,520
But I feel free somehow, like now I can
live those last few moments on my own terms.

335
00:24:17,600 --> 00:24:20,020
To hell with loyalty to Don Krieg.

336
00:24:20,600 --> 00:24:24,740
My devotion to him was just an
escape from forging my own destiny.

337
00:24:26,720 --> 00:24:28,080
Once your heart is set,

338
00:24:28,220 --> 00:24:32,177
and you pursue all your dreams with
every last fiber of what you are,

339
00:24:32,260 --> 00:24:35,378
you will never again feel
lost or hopeless or afraid.

340
00:24:35,600 --> 00:24:38,012
I learned all that from a brave tour boy.

341
00:24:43,060 --> 00:24:44,240
Hey, you guys!

342
00:24:44,500 --> 00:24:46,737
Give him the boat we use
to go grocery shopping!

343
00:24:46,820 --> 00:24:47,650
Come on!

344
00:24:47,733 --> 00:24:48,957
Are you stupid or something?

345
00:24:49,040 --> 00:24:52,497
Why do we have to give a perfectly
good boat to a bunch of pirates?

346
00:24:52,580 --> 00:24:54,877
And what's going to happen
to all our grocery shopping?

347
00:24:54,960 --> 00:24:56,780
Jackass! Hattie's right!

348
00:24:56,980 --> 00:24:59,317
Let them swim wherever they're going to!

349
00:24:59,400 --> 00:25:01,280
Go get that grocery boat now!

350
00:25:05,500 --> 00:25:06,880
Alright, fine!

351
00:25:07,260 --> 00:25:08,420
Stop shouting!

352
00:25:09,540 --> 00:25:11,940
Okay, okay, we'll go get it!

353
00:25:20,140 --> 00:25:21,800
It's gonna sink!

354
00:25:35,640 --> 00:25:37,040
Why did I hesitate?

355
00:25:37,540 --> 00:25:39,360
What was I so worried about?

356
00:25:39,740 --> 00:25:42,799
When I think about it, I
can't help but feel stupid.

357
00:25:57,980 --> 00:26:00,540
Well then, we gratefully accept this boat,

358
00:26:00,660 --> 00:26:03,719
and my right to assume
there's no need to return it.

359
00:26:04,100 --> 00:26:04,930
It's yours.

360
00:26:05,013 --> 00:26:07,468
Don't ever come back
here, not for anything.

361
00:26:07,740 --> 00:26:09,277
Not even to return this boat.

362
00:26:09,360 --> 00:26:10,190
He's right!

363
00:26:10,460 --> 00:26:15,100
And don't you ever forget, this is
the restaurant where the cooks fight!

364
00:26:15,240 --> 00:26:16,100
The Baratier!

365
00:26:18,300 --> 00:26:20,660
The cooks there sure mean business.

366
00:26:37,360 --> 00:26:40,977
As a kid, I never stopped.

367
00:26:41,060 --> 00:26:43,537
Searching for a great treasure!

368
00:26:43,620 --> 00:26:48,337
I had a map in my mind.

369
00:26:48,420 --> 00:26:50,977
That I knew would lead me!

370
00:26:51,060 --> 00:26:55,157
I had to find my way to that place.

371
00:26:55,240 --> 00:26:58,077
Before someone could beat me!

372
00:26:58,160 --> 00:27:02,237
The promised land was in my grasp.

373
00:27:02,320 --> 00:27:04,940
And I wouldn't let go!

374
00:27:06,000 --> 00:27:08,697
La la la la.

375
00:27:08,780 --> 00:27:10,177
My only dream.

376
00:27:10,260 --> 00:27:12,240
La la la la la.

377
00:27:12,860 --> 00:27:17,960
I won't stop chasing
it until it comes true!

378
00:27:19,740 --> 00:27:23,477
But if the world ever changes,

379
00:27:23,560 --> 00:27:26,737
I call out your name!

380
00:27:26,820 --> 00:27:33,260
We could return to the time
when everything's the same.

381
00:27:33,940 --> 00:27:40,200
As long as I'm with you,
my memories won't fade!

382
00:27:41,020 --> 00:27:45,517
Waiting for that one true dream?
